<title>HONG KONG: Cross-Harbour Tunnel year net up 4.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Cross-Harbour Tunnel year net up 4.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   132.0  vs  126.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    37.0   vs  37.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    253.45 vs  241.61</p>
<p>    Turnover		     797.01 vs  768.15</p>
<p>    Company name		 Cross-Harbour Tunnel Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 25 to May 1</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 8</p>
<p>NOTE - Cross-Harbour Tunnel, owned 26.7 percent by Wharf (Holdings) Ltd, operates a road tunnel between Hong Kong Island and the Kowloon Peninsula.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 118 H.K. cents (including first interim dividend of 27 cents, second interim dividend of 27 cents and third interim dividend of 27 cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
